  {
    "sha": "c1fb29298d79c65e7cd0dbf5667e7b274cba945d",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKGMxZmIyOTI5OGQ3OWM2NWU3Y2QwZGJmNTY2N2U3YjI3NGNiYTk0NWQ",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-13T00:39:11Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-13T00:39:11Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(turning): read the lathe holder against steel on its own side\n\nReview of PR #1061: steel_hits read every tip radius and fixture box\nalong the path's signed radial, so a rear holder (a path whose first\npoint sits past centre) had its body mirrored through the axis and a\nstanding jaw on its own side passed. The steel law now takes the\nholder law's sided_pieces (#1102), reads tips and standing boxes along\nthe holder's +x, and refuses a path on both sides of the axis by name.\n\nPins: a rear holder against standing steel like its front mirror; the\nmargin growth (standing and spinning); a jaw on the -y side alone; the\nfinding's move index past move 0; the post gate's unreadable part\nreported by name (lathe_steel_hits). The app suite selects the Fanuc\nLathe post, which main now requires to post a lathe program.\n\nRefs #1037\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
